 \item \textbf{Detection before construction, for different kinds of agent memory.}
 \sys{} configures a store's read path from two closed-form statistics of its bytes, with no model, labels, per-store queries or candidate runs. It re-derives that configuration in seconds as the store grows. The share of numbered lines tells whether the store records an order and only then turns on keep-newest resolution and parent-priority retrieval. The share of text in short records tells whether a finer cut keeps every record whole. The detected structure then sets how hybrid retrieval splits the slots among its channels, and assembly keeps stored order.
