 The compensated refinement branch spans the three parts. Detection takes it for a $4096$-token unit, retrieval searches at $1024$ tokens and selects four times as many units, and assembly shows them one container per parent in stored order. The nominal allowance is unchanged at $40{,}960$ tokens, so the branch raises retrieval resolution rather than buying more reader context (Appendix~\ref{app:hyper}).
 
+\paragraph{The released implementation.} On dot-numbered stores, the SDK groups qualifying records by subject and relation, leaving values out of the slot key. A relation must occur for at least two subjects, with changing subjects averaging at most four records. Other records keep the original slot rule. The question seeds subjects whose current values name further subjects. The read path follows these links for at most four rounds, ranks each round and presents the selected chain in hop order. Across these rounds it reranks at most $400$ walk candidates, in addition to the dense and parent-graph candidates already scored. Other numbering formats keep the original read path. Appendix~\ref{app:hyper} states the evaluation and development conditions.
